B.Wt=new A.dQ("inspect-dishwasher-drain-hose","Look at the drain hose, high-loop, or air gap","This is a look-only check. Unplug before pulling the dishwasher out if the hose is hidden. Do not split a sealed pump. No live electrical testing.","Under the sink, find the dishwasher drain hose. Trace it: it should rise in a high loop on the cabinet side before it goes down to the air-gap cap (chrome cap on the sink, if present) or the disposal inlet. If a disposal was just installed, look into that inlet for a leftover knockout plug. Do not unscrew fittings.","The hose is not crushed or kinked, it rises in a high loop where you can see it, an air-gap cap (if present) is not packed, and a disposal inlet (if used) is not blocked by a leftover knockout.","The hose is kinked or flattened, it sags below the sink rim with no high loop, the air-gap cap is packed, or a new disposal still has its knockout in place. Observation only \u2014 do not cut or re-route plumbing.","dishwasher","dishwasher-drain-hose",B.dA,B.a74,"dishwasher-drain-hose")
B.Wv=new A.dQ("inspect-dishwasher-supply","Look at the supply tap and air-gap cap","Look under the sink. Do not open a sealed pump or split a fill valve. No live electrical testing. Unplug before you later move the dishwasher.","Under the sink, find the dishwasher supply tap (often a small valve on the hot line) and, if your sink has one, the chrome air-gap cap on the counter or sink. The tap handle should be in line with the pipe. The air-gap cap should lift and not be packed with food.","The supply tap looks fully open and the air-gap cap (if present) is clear of debris.","The supply tap is closed or only partly open, or the air-gap cap is packed with food.","dishwasher","dishwasher-supply-open",B.j1,B.iz,"dishwasher-supply-open")
B.lc=s(["clogged-dishwasher-spray-arms"],t.s)
B.Wg=new A.dQ("inspect-dishwasher-spray","Look at the spray-arm holes","Open the door and look. Do not reach inside while it is running. Unplug before you later lift a spray arm. Do not open a sealed pump. No live electrical testing.","With the door open, look along the lower (and upper, if present) spray arm. Holes should be open, not packed with food or mineral crust. Dishes should not be stacked so they block the arm from spinning.","Spray-arm holes look open and the load is not packed against the arms.","Holes look clogged with food, or the load is packed so water cannot reach the dishes.","dishwasher","dishwasher-spray-holes",B.dA,B.lc,"dishwasher-spray-holes")
