B.ah7={"dryer-response":0,"drum-turns":1,"heat-observed":2,"cycle-heat-setting":3,"panel-lights":4,"door-closed-firmly":5,"exterior-airflow":6,"lint-filter-condition":7,"lint-housing-slot":8,"noise-timing":9,"heat-before-failure":10,"door-held-closed-start":11,"vent-hose-condition":12,"wall-plug-seated":13,"motor-audible":14,"running-noise":15,"hazard-observation":16,"breaker-tripped-check":17,"gas-dryer-type":18,"gas-ignition-observed":19,"outlet-power-check":20,"control-lock-status":21,"heat-pattern":22,"door-latch-intermittent":23,"motor-overheat-cooldown":24,"belt-slip-observation":25,"duct-run-length":26,"moisture-sensor-bars":27,"vent-pest-blockage":28,"cabinet-seal-gap":29,"timer-heat-portion":30,"relay-heat-output":31,"load-size-wetness":32,"clothes-feel-after-cycle":33,"clothes-remain-damp":34,"dry-time-change":35,"recent-overheat":36}
B.TY=new A.c_("What the dryer does when you press Start","Close the door normally, select a regular cycle, and press Start once. Watch and listen for about 10 seconds.","Nothing happens points to power/door/start issues. A hum suggests motor load trouble. Normal start means we move to heat and drum checks.",u.B)
B.Us=new A.c_("Whether the drum is tumbling","Start a cycle and look through the door glass or opening. The drum should rotate steadily.","No tumble with motor sound often means a belt issue. Normal tumble with no heat points toward a heating-path problem.","Do not reach into a moving drum. Stop if you hear harsh grinding or smell burning.")
B.Ug=new A.c_("Whether the load is getting warm","Run the dryer on a heat cycle for 2\u20133 minutes with a small load. Open carefully and feel whether clothes or the drum area are warm.","No warmth on a heat cycle supports no-heat modes. Warmth with damp clothes points more toward airflow restriction.","Stop for smoke or sharp electrical/burning smells. Do not open live heater compartments.")
B.U1=new A.c_("Whether a heat cycle is actually selected","Look at the control panel and confirm the cycle is not Air Fluff, Air Dry, or another no-heat setting.","Air-only/fluff selected explains cold tumbling without a parts failure.",u.B)
B.U0=new A.c_("Whether the control panel has power","Press buttons or turn the knob and see whether lights, numbers, or display segments respond.","No lights at all suggests supply/power. Lights on with no start points toward door or start-control issues.","Do not open the console. Stop if the plug, cord, or outlet looks burnt.")
B.Ul=new A.c_("Whether the door latch clicks shut","Close the door with normal pressure until you feel or hear a firm click. Gently pull the handle to see if it stays latched.","A soft close or door that will not stay shut supports a door-switch or latch problem.",u.A)
B.TZ=new A.c_("How strong air is at the outside vent","Check airflow before opening the cabinet. Feel or listen at the hood. Note whether the flap opens. Stay outside \u2014 do not open the dryer cabinet for this check.","Weak or almost no airflow supports vent restriction. Normal airflow argues against a simple vent blockage.","Do not climb on roofs or enter unsafe areas. Stop if the dryer overheats or smells hot.")
B.Un=new A.c_("Condition of the lint filter","Check airflow before opening the cabinet. Pull out only the removable screen and look at it. Do not open panels for this check.","A heavily clogged or missing filter supports lint-path restriction.","Do not wash a filter unless your manual says it is washable.")
B.U7=new A.c_("Lint packed in the filter slot or housing","Unplug the dryer. Pull the lint filter all the way out and look down the slot with a flashlight. Note packed lint on the walls \u2014 do not dismantle the cabinet.","Packed housing lint supports a clogged lint pathway even when the screen itself looks clean.","Stop if you would need to open sealed panels or wiring. Unplug first.")
B.TX=new A.c_("Whether noise follows the drum or starts after warmup","Run a light or empty tumble and listen. A repeating thump in time with the drum is different from a sharp squeal that begins after a few minutes.","Drum-timed thump/rumble supports worn rollers. A delayed sharp squeal supports idler pulley wear.",u.g1)
B.TW=new A.c_("Whether heat was present before this complaint","Think back to recent loads on a heat cycle \u2014 not air-only / fluff. Did it heat normally, then go cold after a very hot run or vent issue, or has this complaint always been cold?","Always-cold with no overheat story favors a failed heating element. Heat that vanished after overheating or a clogged vent favors an open thermal fuse. Do not test live heater wiring.","Do not meter live circuits or bypass a thermal fuse. Stop for smoke or burning smell.")
B.Um=new A.c_("Whether Start works only while holding the door closed","Close the door and hold it firmly shut with your hand. Press Start. Do not tape, jumper, or defeat the door switch.","Starting only while you hold the door closed supports a door switch or strike problem. Starting normally without holding argues against it.",u.A)
B.TU=new A.c_("Whether the visible vent hose is restricted","Check airflow before opening the cabinet. Unplug if you need to roll the dryer. Check the visible hose only. Do not open the cabinet for this check.",u.Z,"Unplug before moving the dryer. Do not puncture or dismantle hidden vent runs inside walls.")
B.Uk=new A.c_("Whether the wall plug is fully seated","With dry hands, look at the plug and outlet from the outside only. Confirm the plug is pushed fully in and the cord looks undamaged.","A loose or damaged plug supports a supply-connection issue. A normal seated plug makes supply less likely.","Do not measure live voltage or open the terminal block. Stop for hot plugs, discolored outlets, or burning smell.")
B.TV=new A.c_("What the motor sounds like when trying to start","Press Start and listen for about 10 seconds. Note clear running sound, hum/struggle only, or silence.","Clear motor sound with a still drum supports a belt issue. Hum/struggle supports motor load failure.","Do not keep hammering Start if the motor only hums and smells hot.")
B.Ut=new A.c_("Unusual sounds while the dryer runs","Run a normal tumble cycle and listen for squeal, thump, grind, or hum.","Squeal often points to idler/belt path wear. Thump suggests drum supports. Grind may mean blower or mechanical damage.",u.g1)
B.U2=new A.c_("Immediate hazard signs","Stop using the dryer. Note whether you smell burning, see smoke, or hear sparking.","Any yes answer is a hard stop \u2014 do not continue DIY diagnosis.","Unplug or switch off the breaker immediately. Do not restart to test.")
B.Uq=new A.c_("Whether the dryer breaker is tripped","Locate the dryer circuit breaker in the home panel. Look at the handle only. Do not remove the panel cover. Note if the handle is in the middle/off position or clearly tripped.","A tripped breaker supports supply interruption. Both poles on supports a different cause than a missing 240V leg.","Look at the breaker handle only. Do not remove the electrical-panel cover. Call a professional for panel work, warm breakers, or burning smell.")
B.Up=new A.c_("Whether this is a gas or electric dryer","Check the back of the dryer or your manual. Gas dryers have a gas line and vent; electric dryers have a thick cord to a 240V outlet only.","Gas dryers with no heat need a different path than electric no-heat checks. Gas ignition work is not beginner DIY.",u.B)
B.TR=new A.c_("Whether the gas burner ignites on a heat cycle","On a heat cycle with the drum turning, stay outside the cabinet and feel whether the load or exhaust air warms within a few minutes. Do not open the burner compartment or gas lines, and do not look for a flame inside.","No flame on a gas heat cycle supports professional gas ignition service \u2014 not DIY repair.","If you smell gas, stop use, ventilate, leave the area, and follow gas emergency procedures. Never attempt gas ignition repair yourself.")
B.Uf=new A.c_("Whether the outlet appears to have power","With dry hands, check whether another known-good device works in the same outlet, or whether the dryer panel shows any lights when plugged in.","A dead outlet supports supply faults. Power at the outlet with no heat points elsewhere.","Do not measure live voltage. Stop for hot outlets, discolored plugs, or burning smell.")
B.Ub=new A.c_("Whether a control or child lock is engaged","Look for a lock icon on the panel. Hold the lock button per your manual for 3\u20135 seconds to release, then try Start again.","An engaged lock explains a dryer that will not respond to Start.",u.B)
B.Uc=new A.c_("How the load feels after a heat cycle","Run the dryer on a heat cycle for a few minutes with a typical load. Open carefully and note whether clothes are cold, partly warm but damp, overhot, or normally warm and drying.","No heat points toward heating-path faults. Partly warm but damp points toward airflow restriction. Too hot points toward overheat protection. Normal warmth argues against those paths.",u.b3)
B.U9=new A.c_("Whether the door latch is intermittent","Close the door several times with normal pressure. Note whether the click and Start response are consistent or sometimes fail.","Intermittent latch failure supports a worn latch or switch path.","Never bypass the door safety interlock.")
B.Ud=new A.c_("Whether the dryer stops mid-cycle and restarts after cooling","Note if the dryer runs then stops on its own, and whether it will start again after 30\u201360 minutes of rest.","Stop-then-restart-after-cooldown supports motor thermal protection.","Do not repeatedly hammer Start on a hot motor. Stop for burning smell or smoke.")
B.Ua=new A.c_("Whether the drum slips or turns slowly","Start a cycle and watch the drum. Note if it turns slowly, slips under load, or smells like burning rubber.","Slipping with motor sound supports a worn belt rather than a fully broken one.","Stop for burning rubber smell or smoke.")
B.U6=new A.c_("Whether the vent run is unusually long or complex","Estimate the visible vent path from the dryer to the exterior hood. Note if it is a long run, has many elbows, or uses crushed flexible duct.","Excessive length or crush supports slow-dry airflow restriction.","Do not cut into walls to inspect hidden duct.")
B.Uh=new A.c_("Condition of moisture sensor bars","Open the drum and look for metal bars inside the drum (often near the filter area). Wipe them with a soft cloth dampened with rubbing alcohol if coated.","Contaminated bars can cause early cycle termination on auto-dry.",u.B)
B.Uu=new A.c_("Whether the exterior vent is blocked by pests or debris","At the exterior hood, look for nests, lint plugs, or debris blocking the flap. Clear only what you can reach safely from the ground.","A blocked hood supports restricted exhaust even when the interior hose looks fine.","Do not enter unsafe roof or crawl areas.")
B.Ue=new A.c_("Whether the door or cabinet seal leaks air","With the dryer running, feel around the door gasket and cabinet edges for unexpected hot air escaping.","Air leaks reduce effective exhaust and can mimic vent restriction.",u.B)
B.U_=new A.c_("Whether the timer advances through a heat portion","On a timed heat cycle, watch whether the timer moves and whether warmth occurs during the expected heat segment.","Timer advancing with no heat segment supports timer or heat-path control faults.",u.B)
B.TS=new A.c_("Whether heat output responds when the cycle calls for heat","On a heat cycle, listen for relay clicks and feel for warmth during the heat portion. Do not open control compartments.","No heat with an active panel and heat cycle can support relay/control output faults.","Do not open live control compartments. Stop for burning electrical smell.")
B.Uo=new A.c_("Load size and wetness compared with normal","Compare the current load to a typical load. Note if it is very large, soaking wet, or mixed heavy/light items.","Oversized or very wet loads extend dry time without a parts failure.",u.B)
B.U3=new A.c_("How clothes felt when you took them out","Think back to when you took the clothes out \u2014 not the instant the cycle ended. Were they cold and damp, warm but damp, dry but unusually hot, or dry and normal?","Cold and damp supports no-heat paths. Warm but damp supports airflow restriction. Dry but unusually hot supports ongoing excess heat.",u.B)
B.Uj=new A.c_("Whether clothes remain damp after the cycle","When you took clothes out after a typical cycle, note whether items were still damp. You do not need to open the dryer the instant the cycle ends.","Persistent dampness supports airflow or heat problems depending on warmth.",u.B)
B.U5=new A.c_("Whether dry times have changed recently","Compare a typical load today with what you expect. Note if cycles run much longer or only slightly longer than before.","Much longer dry times support restricted airflow. Slight changes may fit load or sensor issues.",u.B)
B.U4=new A.c_("Whether the dryer recently ran very hot or shut off from heat","Recall the last few runs. Did the cabinet feel unusually hot, or did the cycle stop early because of heat?","A recent overheat episode supports thermal fuse or high-limit paths. Answering no only weakens an overheat-then-no-heat fuse story; it does not by itself confirm a failed heating element.","Stop for active smoke or burning smell.")
